<title>SWITZERLAND: No decision yet on Swiss pension fund manager.</title>
<headline>No decision yet on Swiss pension fund manager.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Swiss AHV public pension fund will decide on July 1 which bank will get the first mandate to manage part of its funds, AHV managing director Joseph Hochstaetter said, denying it had already picked UBS.</p>
<p>He told Reuters AHV wanted to invest 500 million Swiss francs in both Swiss stocks and in foreign currency bonds in the course of 1997, probably in several tranches.</p>
<p>No decision has been made yet about a particular manager or an amount it would manage, he said in response to a press report UBS had got the nod.</p>
<p>-- Zurich newsroom +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
